{"title":"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6a0f9596d7b4885ccb4e6f485a6bd81c411945a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau (n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> denote the number of positive integer <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisor\" title=\"Divisor\">divisors</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> including 1 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/4/9549485daeb6d502f812df0678887957d2928e19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau (1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/aca9893eea49fb2ff767e4833a44ff8d85deb5cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(6) =4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" /> Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94e3717f6d97575b27aca7300f69726d78025cfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)=\\tau(1)+ \\tau(2) + \\cdots + \\tau(n).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"254\" height=\"18\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> denote the number of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8b152bb13dcb8222a1746b2c2f52562cd5947de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leq 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Odd_integer\" title=\"Odd integer\"> odd</a>, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> denote the number of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8b152bb13dcb8222a1746b2c2f52562cd5947de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leq 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Even_integer\" title=\"Even integer\"> even</a>. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e718b7ee9c6b2f65062a6baa3eeb6d38a2c375c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a-b|.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is well-known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456f051f0d6a8b0f2745b1cd63a4b26003858880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is odd if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_square\" title=\"Perfect square\">perfect square</a>.  (Otherwise, we can group <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisor\" title=\"Divisor\">divisors</a> into pairs whose product is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.)  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is odd if and only if there are an odd number of perfect squares less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80c7b9fbbee3d848396311f5ed7006accae91d20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(1), S(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8f7c699e2cd7f31696018f03c14477942840897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> are odd, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08f05e7446ed89f28454be581d2bc0d6d0fdc43d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(4), S(5), \\ldots, S(8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" /> are even, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/1/931e4d22586a039f327fc4f7b09b374ff6e6ad16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(9), \\ldots, S(15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" /> are odd, and so on. \n</p><p>So, for a given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, if we choose the positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f61ad04b9c8a649966ddd3ec8c2c544efa37113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 \\leq n &lt; (m + 1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"19\" /> we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> has the same parity as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.  \n</p><p>It follows that the numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c716d1dc907ae6b51cb0f545664c89d58b6b67d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a35631e1e126934ead6d2af161e9d250827bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/819068968ed60608a91d0c3921d6296964660e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/6/a66c53514f5e6b6b6d096fe617320424b897b479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />, and so on, all the way up to the numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/335cdfb75a4b8f00db468a2d680c849c8e41b165.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$43^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dc3df5b561e3a539b0bf3e7fddc9748f1c0826a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44^2 = 1936$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> odd. These are the only such numbers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5b442c275b4324f100c365b774e872b6b21f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e977d6dbc6ae2f7d388c024042992931745a3218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^2 = 2025 &gt; 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"146\" height=\"15\" />).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the difference between consecutive squares are consecutively increasing odd numbers. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (inclusive) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (exclusive), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and so on. The number of numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128328cd49de5eec06e04d25ae0a4fea53cffe83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + 1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7ade51ffa609b4b37e4373657aa66e8483aaa942.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + 1 - n)(n + 1 + n) = 2n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"253\" height=\"18\" />. Whenever the lowest square beneath a number is odd, the parity will be odd, and the same for even. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bdbe484939acf3d6a98aa3b93af6253a2fa1218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = [2(1) + 1] + [2(3) + 1] \\ldots [2(43) + 1] = 3 + 7 + 11 \\ldots 87$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"464\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/4184fc85b04350003e3c28ed8c3dcfca3ea4181c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = [2(2) + 1] + [2(4) + 1] \\ldots [2(42) + 1] + 70 = 5 + 9 \\ldots 85 + 70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"502\" height=\"18\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> accounting for the difference between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5b442c275b4324f100c365b774e872b6b21f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dc3df5b561e3a539b0bf3e7fddc9748f1c0826a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44^2 = 1936$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, inclusive. Notice that if we align the two and subtract, we get that each difference is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53ee5dcdfe5920f5d694af59e7d7d07ec1f36133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a - b| = |b - a| = |2 \\cdot 21 + 70 - 87| = \\boxed{025}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"342\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d0e4450132b6338a39a225b797eb29caf0f21a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = (3^2 - 2^2) + (5^2 - 4^2) + \\ldots + (45^2 - 44^2) - 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"386\" height=\"19\" />, where the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c1aa7db025fb1513f98fb323abbf541a811ab5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" /> accounts for those numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5b442c275b4324f100c365b774e872b6b21f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2af3f788b0b6d3e460152a350c2183c7a3ffcc2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = (2^2 - 1^2) + (4^2 - 3^2) + \\ldots + (44^2 - 43^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"346\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/3/ae38db98124d94cfe0a5a96bfd0a96bab37da8a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a - b| = |2(2^2 + 4^2 + \\ldots + 44^2) - 2(1^2 + 3^2 + 5^2 + \\ldots 43^2) + 1^2 - 45^2 + 19|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"594\" height=\"21\" />.\nWe can apply the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/d/fbdf6037570288549aa0e7bbe41420b4760866b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2 + 2^2 + \\ldots + n^2 = \\frac{n(n + 1)(2n + 1)}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"298\" height=\"38\" />.  From this formula, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c0102f91a328adce709e26d342ee388f8b695307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2 + 4^2 + \\ldots + (2n)^2 = \\frac{2n(n + 1)(2n + 1)}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"331\" height=\"38\" /> and so that \n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/a/03a548381fa035d6faa63fc8738b361e47842658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2 + 3^2 + \\ldots +(2n + 1)^2 = (1^2 + 2^2 + \\ldots +(2n + 1)^2) - (2^2 + 4^2 + \\ldots + (2n)^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"623\" height=\"19\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/9/9d9dbcd560238974f2bd92fa8cab0adb50d23c95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{(2n + 1)(2n + 2)(4n + 3)}{6} - \\frac{2n(n + 1)(2n + 1)}{3} = \\frac{(n + 1)(2n + 1)(2n + 3)}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"601\" height=\"38\" />.  Thus,</dd></dl>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f7bbf8eaad40635fa38b63246418312ff69a409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a - b| = \\left| 2\\cdot \\frac{44\\cdot23\\cdot45}{3} - 2\\cdot \\frac{22 \\cdot 43 \\cdot 45}{3} - 45^2 + 20\\right| = |-25| =\\boxed{025}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"548\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/2/a327109b6ab5884d9aa43c3e0bfb84ae11989de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> denote the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf421fcd6a7d1f87588f998459239009d53781d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+ \\dots +n-1+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"212\" height=\"14\" />. We can easily see from the fact \"It is well-known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456f051f0d6a8b0f2745b1cd63a4b26003858880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is odd if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a perfect square.\", that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/4/cb405de6b3e0ccb234355060b3639565da32fbde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = (2^2-1^2) + (4^2-3^2) \\dots (44^2 - 43^2) = (2+1)(2-1)+(4+3)(4-3) \\dots (44+43)(44-43) = 1+2+3...44 = \\Delta 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"933\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d90eb6359799eb42fb33cdd1080e0fa9eee11b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 3^2-2^2+5^2-4^2...2006-44^2 = (3+2)(3-2) \\dots (43+42)(43-42) + 1 + (2005 - 44^2) = \\Delta 43 + 69$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"819\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/2522de2d20f424138c818d11842cd32778d5ddd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b = \\Delta 44-\\Delta 43-69 = 44-69 = -25$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"331\" height=\"13\" />. They ask for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/3311eba472bf7dc846f58d649d3756cf443eb108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a-b|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4c65a1c2cfb86cf79f250102135c01fdce3edb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|-25| = \\boxed{025}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"115\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>-Alexlikemath\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We list out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717a784eea35ac41d57c32cb53f2d51dd319be81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(1), S(2)...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" /> and find that there is a pattern. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/925f778b3aa1eb57dd9343c4999f8e9507761ee2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(1-3)=odd$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f216bf199da051788f40c7939c237b3987319ebd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(4-8)=even$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2faabef89bf69b79fd79742e84310fde8b94a0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(9-15)=odd$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />, and so on. We observe that the groupings of odd sums and even sums are broken up at every odd number. In that case, we need to find when the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/4966aeaab6acbceb34fe5658fa971c458cd2cae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,5,7,9...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" /> has a sum greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5b442c275b4324f100c365b774e872b6b21f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />. We test values and find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e609f93104b193a2355181ca62ff083ea9fd3821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is the greatest value in the sequence. At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e609f93104b193a2355181ca62ff083ea9fd3821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, the sum will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e609f93104b193a2355181ca62ff083ea9fd3821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, the sequence will have an odd number of terms, and therefore the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e609f93104b193a2355181ca62ff083ea9fd3821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> terms will be even. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d44fe9de8f97b8376c974e481853cf18a3f9884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(1935-2024)=even$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" />; however, we only care about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/5/9452daedb10138ae2cc621ab6adc59f8ca85768b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1935-2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" />. These are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> even sums; we can add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> after finding the number of even sums less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/6184f03128b60c6d13c71ad8bd2871baecbd3f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1935$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, which is the sum of the sequence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bce4861794639dfce62459a451b732d049b61e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,9,13, 13,\\dots, 85$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"17\" />. The sum of this sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e05183591ae79c18d00b9e4f83bceaf56b28c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$945$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />; we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to find that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/4/cb4e4e60e966fbad3ebb1813941be7543ff52dbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$945+70=1015$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> even sums. This means there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/404b48a4ae33b33c0c11ab63a6258b91251111e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$990$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> odd sums. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fcd341b6d63f91d561a949a40e4375795511e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|990-1015|=\\boxed{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"152\" height=\"25\" />.\n~jamespudi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I\" title=\"2005 AIME I\">2005 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2005\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017204231\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.